{
  "schema": "demon-attack.bank-recipe/v1",
  "comment": "The CC0 sample bank's recipe (adaptive-soundtrack design §11.4, §12.9; task 8.5). tools/bank/bank_build.lua reads it with the pin manifest (plan/sample-bank-pins.manifest.tsv) and the SFZ keycenters (art/music/bank/sfz-keys.json), cuts each listed file into one zone (note, velocity layer, round robin), and writes web/audio/bank/bank.json plus one Opus sprite per load tier. Velocity splits, trims, gains and stretches are our judgement (tune by ear, task 9.7); pitches come from the SFZ maps, the pins doc (plan/sample-bank-pins.md §6) or the file name, and the builder confirms each with an f0 estimate. Instruments are tried in order for a note: the first whose roles and `when` match and whose zones cover the pitch plays it. Role levels are matched to the synth voices the operator approved: each role soloed over nine sections in both modes, the level moved by the median loudness gap (guitars were within 1 dB and keep 0.5; plan/render-runs/sample-bank.md §6). Re-matched after the fidelity audit (design §12.11, plan/render-runs/sample-bank.md §8): the sampled bass now plays on a clean bus, so its level is +6 dB (the median gap over five sections, 3.7 -> 7.35) and it no longer drives a shaper; brass +1.0 dB and bells +2.2 dB after the mono pick changed their sources (one microphone instead of the comb-filtered sum).",
  "manifest": "plan/sample-bank-pins.manifest.tsv",
  "keys": "art/music/bank/sfz-keys.json",
  "out": "web/audio/bank",
  "rate": 48000,
  "kbps": { "1": 64, "2": 96 },
  "gapSeconds": 0.05,
  "peakDb": -1,
  "fadeSeconds": 0.02,
  "oggOverhead": 0.02,
  "budgets": { "opusBytes": 6000000, "decodedDesktop": 72000000, "decodedPhone": 24000000 },
