      "parse": { "note": "^(%a+%d)_", "rr": "_rr(%d+)" }, "root": "map", "shift": -12, "verify": "report", "stretch": [4, 3],
      "trim": 0.4, "kbps": 160, "declip": true, "channels": 1, "tier": 1, "release": 0.04,
      "why": "shift -12, confirmed by measurement (plan/render-runs/sample-bank.md): every bass-sus zone sounds within 0.4 semitone of its map keycenter -12, with no partials an octave lower. verify report, not strict: a 0.4 s staccato trim is too short for the spectral check at 35-160 Hz (7 of 20 zones read noise); the full source files measure within 0.6 semitone, and the map is the sustains' map" },
